# Example 13: sequence conservation, ConSurf grammar with a better palette.
#
# ConSurf's conventions are good and worth keeping: nine percentile grades
# rather than a raw continuous score, variable to conserved read as a
# single direction, a separate neutral category for residues with too
# little data, and a surface render so the conserved patches show up as
# surface patches rather than buried ribbon.
#
# What we change is the palette. ConSurf ships turquoise through white to
# maroon, which is hard to read at the pale end and is not color-blind
# safe. We use ColorBrewer BrBG reversed: teal for variable, cream in the
# middle, brown for conserved. Same direction, same nine steps, safe under
# all three common forms of color blindness, and it still reads in
# grayscale because it is monotonic in lightness from each end.
#
# Prerequisite, run once:  ./build_alignment.sh
# That fetches Cas9 orthologs from UniProt and aligns them with MAFFT.
#
# Conservation is a property of the sequence set, not of the protein.
# This one is 117 Cas9-family orthologs of 1200-1500 residues. A set of
# close Streptococcus relatives would give a different and equally valid
# answer. Always state the set in the caption.
open 4oo8
delete /D-F
open ../../palettes/lab_colors.cxc
open ../../presets/Base/publication_white.cxc

open cas9_orthologs.afa

# Associate with the SpCas9 sequence explicitly. Left to itself ChimeraX
# picks the best-scoring sequence in the alignment, which here is a
# Staphylococcus entry, and the conservation would be mapped through the
# wrong column numbering.
sequence disassociate #1/A cas9_orthologs.afa
sequence associate #1/A cas9_orthologs.afa:1
sequence refreshAttrs cas9_orthologs.afa

runscript compute_grades.py
open consurf_grade.defattr

# Nine discrete grades. colorTreatment distinct in the key, and a
# value,color palette here, so no interpolation blurs the bin edges.
color byattribute r:consurfGrade /A palette "0,#BFBFBF:1,#01665E:2,#35978F:3,#80CDC1:4,#C7EAE5:5,#F5F0E4:6,#F6E8C3:7,#DFC27D:8,#BF812D:9,#8C510A" range 0,9

# Nucleic acids neutral: conservation is the subject
color /B,C lab_gray_p

view
turn y 30
view pad 0.05

key "#01665E:variable" #35978F: #80CDC1: #C7EAE5: #F5F0E4: #F6E8C3: #DFC27D: #BF812D: "#8C510A:conserved" pos 0.04,0.32 size 0.03,0.36 fontSize 16 colorTreatment distinct labelSide right/bottom
2dlabels text "conservation grade" xpos 0.03 ypos 0.74 size 17 color lab_black bold true
2dlabels text "117 Cas9 orthologs" xpos 0.03 ypos 0.70 size 15 color lab_gray
2dlabels text "SpCas9  4OO8" xpos 0.03 ypos 0.04 size 18 color lab_gray
save conservation_cartoon.png width 3000 supersample 3

# Surface panel: ConSurf's default view, and the one that actually answers
# "is the conserved patch on the outside where something could bind"
hide /A cartoons
surface /A
color byattribute r:consurfGrade /A palette "0,#BFBFBF:1,#01665E:2,#35978F:3,#80CDC1:4,#C7EAE5:5,#F5F0E4:6,#F6E8C3:7,#DFC27D:8,#BF812D:9,#8C510A" range 0,9 target s
save conservation_surface.png width 3000 supersample 3
